Zero-fill the K tail tile instead of leaving it unwritten

page_produce_kv and its scale-factor twin load a partial KV tile with
kNoFill for K, so the out-of-range rows of the last tile keep whatever the
previous kernel on that SM left in shared memory. Nothing clears shared
memory between kernels, so those rows can decode to NaN or Inf.

The existing argument for K being safe is that logits_mask replaces the
resulting scores before update_mdo_states sees them. That holds only while
every out-of-range position is covered by a mask that overwrites rather
than adds, which is a property of three separate call sites. Zero-filling
K costs one predicated cp.async on the tail tile only and removes the
dependency.

Re-derived for 0.6.16 -> 0.6.18: 0.6.18 restructured page_produce_kv_sf around
the FLASHINFER_PAGED_V_SF_DESWIZZLE branch, so the K/V fill-mode choice now sits
in the else branch. The de-swizzle branch already stores a zero-initialised
value for out-of-range rows, so only the else branch needs the change. Every
other hunk is the 0.6.16 hunk at a new offset.

